{"id":"presentation-data","statement":"A presentation consists of two maps p₀,p₁ : Rel → Word Gen.","local":["GroupPresentation.Presentation","GroupPresentation.Word","GroupPresentation.Signed"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation.agda","kind":"local definition","upstream":["Cubical.Data.List"]}
{"id":"generator-space","statement":"GeneratorSpace Gen is Susp (Unit* ⊎ Gen), with generatorLoop g = merid(g) · merid(reference)⁻¹.","local":["GroupPresentation.GeneratorInput","GroupPresentation.GeneratorSpace","GroupPresentation.generatorLoop"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation.agda","kind":"local definition","upstream":["Cubical.HITs.Susp.Base.Susp","Cubical.HITs.Susp.Base.north","Cubical.HITs.Susp.Base.merid"]}
{"id":"word-semantics","statement":"Signed words evaluate to north-based paths by letterLoop and wordLoop.","local":["GroupPresentation.letterLoop","GroupPresentation.wordLoop","GroupPresentation.relationLoop"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation.agda","kind":"local definition","upstream":["Cubical.Foundations.Prelude._∙_","Cubical.Data.List"]}
{"id":"presentation-pushout","statement":"PresentationPushout P is the pushout of the relation-circle attaching map and relation projection; BG_pres P is its 1-truncation.","local":["GroupPresentation.attachingMap","GroupPresentation.PresentationPushout","GroupPresentation.BG_pres","GroupPresentation.BG-basepoint"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation.agda","kind":"local definition","upstream":["Cubical.HITs.S1.Base.S¹","Cubical.HITs.Pushout.Base.Pushout","Cubical.HITs.Truncation.hLevelTrunc"]}
{"id":"relation-null-pushout","statement":"Every relation loop becomes refl after the left pushout inclusion.","local":["GroupPresentation.Relations.relationCircleNaturality","GroupPresentation.Relations.conjugacyToRefl","GroupPresentation.Relations.inlRelationLoop-null"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/Relations.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.HITs.Pushout.Base.push","Cubical.Foundations.Function.homotopyNatural","Cubical.Foundations.GroupoidLaws"]}
{"id":"relation-sides-pushout","statement":"The two word loops of each relation agree after the left pushout inclusion.","local":["GroupPresentation.Relations.inlRelationDifference","GroupPresentation.Relations.differenceNullToEqual","GroupPresentation.Relations.inlRelationSidesAgree"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/Relations.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.Foundations.GroupoidLaws"]}
{"id":"relation-null-truncated","statement":"Every relation loop is null after the canonical map GeneratorSpace Gen → BG_pres P.","local":["GroupPresentation.TruncatedRelations.generatorSpaceToBG","GroupPresentation.TruncatedRelations.BG-relationLoop-null","GroupPresentation.TruncatedRelations.BG-relationSidesAgree"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/TruncatedRelations.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.HITs.Truncation._∣_∣ₕ"]}
{"id":"connectedness","statement":"BG_pres P satisfies isConnected 2.","local":["GroupPresentation.Connectedness.generatorSpaceMerePathToNorth","GroupPresentation.Connectedness.presentationPushoutMerePathToBase","GroupPresentation.Connectedness.BG-pres-isConnected"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/Connectedness.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.HITs.Pushout.Properties.elimProp","Cubical.HITs.PropositionalTruncation","Cubical.HITs.Truncation"]}
{"id":"fundamental-group","statement":"BG-π₁ P is the library fundamental group at BG-basepoint, and each relation loop class is the identity.","local":["GroupPresentation.FundamentalGroup.BG-π₁","GroupPresentation.FundamentalGroup.relationLoopπ₁-null"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/FundamentalGroup.agda","kind":"local definition and theorem","upstream":["Cubical.Homotopy.Group.Base.πGr","Cubical.HITs.SetTruncation.Base"]}
{"id":"presented-group","statement":"PresentedGroup P is the lifted free group modulo the locally constructed normal closure of relation differences.","local":["GroupPresentation.PresentedGroup.PresentationFreeGroup","GroupPresentation.PresentedGroup.relationDifference","GroupPresentation.PresentedGroup.NormalClosure.normalSubgroup","GroupPresentation.PresentedGroup.PresentedGroup"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/PresentedGroup.agda","kind":"local definition","upstream":["Cubical.HITs.FreeGroup.Properties.freeGroupGroup","Cubical.Algebra.Group.QuotientGroup"]}
{"id":"normal-closure-minimality","statement":"The local normal closure is contained in every normal subgroup containing the listed relation differences.","local":["GroupPresentation.PresentedGroup.NormalClosure.least","GroupPresentation.PresentedGroup.relationDifferenceInNormalClosure"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/PresentedGroup.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.Algebra.Group.Subgroup","Cubical.HITs.PropositionalTruncation"]}
{"id":"canonical-hom","statement":"The free-generator loop map kills the normal closure and factors to canonicalPresentationHom : PresentedGroup P → BG-π₁ P.","local":["GroupPresentation.PresentationHom.freeGroupToBG-π₁","GroupPresentation.PresentationHom.relationDifferenceToBG-π₁-null","GroupPresentation.PresentationHom.presentationNormalSubgroupInKernel","GroupPresentation.PresentationHom.canonicalPresentationHom"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/PresentationHom.agda","kind":"local theorem and definition","upstream":["Cubical.HITs.FreeGroup.Properties.rec","Cubical.Algebra.Group.QuotientGroup.kerSubgroup","Cubical.HITs.SetQuotients.Properties.SetQuot.rec"]}
{"id":"pushout-pi1-surjectivity","statement":"The lifted left inclusion into PresentationPushout P is surjective on π₁.","local":["GroupPresentation.Surjectivity.relationProjection-isConnected","GroupPresentation.Surjectivity.inlPresentation↑-isConnected","GroupPresentation.Surjectivity.inlPresentation↑-π₁-surjective"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/Surjectivity.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.Homotopy.Connected.inlConnected","Cubical.Homotopy.Group.Properties.connectedFun→πSurj"]}
{"id":"bouquet-surjectivity","statement":"The free-group homomorphism a ↦ |loop a|₂ onto the bouquet fundamental group is surjective.","local":["GroupPresentation.BouquetFundamentalGroup.bouquetLoopHom","GroupPresentation.BouquetFundamentalGroup.bouquetLoopHom-surjective"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/BouquetFundamentalGroup.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.HITs.Bouquet.FundamentalGroupProof.loopingT","Cubical.HITs.Bouquet.FundamentalGroupProof.windingT","Cubical.HITs.Bouquet.FundamentalGroupProof.left-homotopy","Cubical.HITs.FreeGroupoid.Properties.forgetfulHom⁻¹"]}
{"id":"generator-bouquet-equivalence","statement":"GeneratorSpace Gen is pointed-equivalent to Bouquet Gen, with generator-loop computation and a lifted analogue.","local":["GroupPresentation.GeneratorBouquet.generatorSpace≃∙Bouquet","GroupPresentation.GeneratorBouquet.generatorLoop-toBouquet","GroupPresentation.GeneratorBouquet.liftedGeneratorSpace≃∙Bouquet"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/GeneratorBouquet.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.HITs.Bouquet.Base.Bouquet","Cubical.Foundations.Pointed"]}
{"id":"truncation-pi1-surjectivity","statement":"The π₁ homomorphism induced by the pointed 3-truncation constructor is surjective.","local":["GroupPresentation.TruncationNaturality.truncation∙","GroupPresentation.TruncationNaturality.truncationπ₁-surjective"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/TruncationNaturality.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.HITs.Truncation.Properties.PathIdTruncIso","Cubical.Homotopy.Group.Base.πHom"]}
{"id":"canonical-surjectivity","statement":"canonicalPresentationHom P is surjective for every P : Presentation Gen Rel.","local":["GroupPresentation.CanonicalSurjectivity.freeGroupToBG-π₁-surjective","GroupPresentation.CanonicalSurjectivity.canonicalPresentationHom-surjective"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/CanonicalSurjectivity.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.HITs.FreeGroup.Properties.freeGroupHom≡","Cubical.Algebra.Group.MorphismProperties.compSurjective","Cubical.Algebra.Group.QuotientGroup.[_]/G"]}
{"id":"public-api","statement":"The public interface re-exports the presentation construction, truncated relation coherence, canonical homomorphism, and its surjectivity without adding mathematical content.","local":["GroupPresentation.PublicAPI.PresentedBG","GroupPresentation.PublicAPI.relationPath","GroupPresentation.PublicAPI.canonicalHom","GroupPresentation.PublicAPI.canonicalHom-surjective"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/PublicAPI.agda","kind":"local interface","upstream":[]}
{"id":"examples","statement":"The example module constructs one-generator presentations and their canonical homomorphisms, without identifying the resulting fundamental groups with externally named groups.","local":["GroupPresentation.Examples.freeRankOnePresentation","GroupPresentation.Examples.cyclicTwoPresentation","GroupPresentation.Examples.cyclicTwoRelationNull"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/Examples.agda","kind":"local examples","upstream":[]}
{"id":"kernel-reduction","statement":"A reverse containment of the free-group kernel in the presentation normal closure would imply injectivity of canonicalPresentationHom; no inhabitant of that containment is constructed.","local":["GroupPresentation.KernelReduction.FreeKernelContainedInNormalClosure","GroupPresentation.KernelReduction.canonicalPresentationHom-injective-from-freeKernel"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/KernelReduction.agda","kind":"conditional local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.HITs.SetQuotients.Properties"]}
{"id":"br3-instance","statement":"The standard two-generator, one-relation Br(3) presentation is instantiated in the generic construction; its braid words are path-coherent in the truncated presented space and the canonical homomorphism is specialized as surjective.","local":["GroupPresentation.Br3.Br3Presentation","GroupPresentation.Br3.Br3PresentationPushout","GroupPresentation.Br3.Br3PresentedSpace","GroupPresentation.Br3.Br3BraidRelationCoherence","GroupPresentation.Br3.Br3CanonicalHom-surjective"],"source":"src/GroupPresentation/Br3.agda","kind":"local concrete instance","upstream":[]}
{"id":"left-actions-and-torsors","statement":"LeftAction gives a set-level left action; IsLeftTorsor requires merely inhabited carrier and contractible transporter types Σ g, act g x ≡ y.","local":["TorsorDelooping.LeftAction.LeftAction","TorsorDelooping.LeftTorsor.IsLeftTorsor","TorsorDelooping.LeftTorsor.LeftTorsor"],"source":"src/TorsorDelooping/{LeftAction,LeftTorsor}.agda","kind":"local definitions","upstream":["Cubical.Algebra.Group.Base","Cubical.Foundations.HLevels","Cubical.HITs.PropositionalTruncation"]}
{"id":"regular-left-torsor","statement":"The group acting on itself by left multiplication is a left torsor.","local":["TorsorDelooping.Regular.regularLeftAction","TorsorDelooping.Regular.regularLeftTorsor"],"source":"src/TorsorDelooping/Regular.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.Algebra.Group.Properties.·GroupAutomorphismR"]}
{"id":"torsor-morphisms","statement":"Equivariant maps have identities and composition; every equivariant map between left torsors is an equivalence.","local":["TorsorDelooping.Morphisms.equivariant-id","TorsorDelooping.Morphisms.equivariant-comp","TorsorDelooping.Morphisms.equivariantMapIsEquiv"],"source":"src/TorsorDelooping/Morphisms.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.Foundations.Equiv","Cubical.HITs.PropositionalTruncation"]}
{"id":"torsor-moduli-sip","statement":"LeftTorsorModuli is the structured moduli type of left torsors, with paths equivalent to equivariant equivalences by SIP.","local":["TorsorDelooping.Moduli.LeftTorsorModuli","TorsorDelooping.Moduli.torsorPathEquiv"],"source":"src/TorsorDelooping/Moduli.agda","kind":"local definition and theorem","upstream":["Cubical.Foundations.SIP.SIP","Cubical.Structures.LeftAction","Cubical.Structures.Axioms"]}
{"id":"torsor-loop-delooping","statement":"The torsor moduli is connected and a 1-type, and its regular-basepoint loop type is equivalent to the carrier of G as a type.","local":["TorsorDelooping.Delooping.isConnectedLeftTorsorModuli","TorsorDelooping.Delooping.isGroupoidLeftTorsorModuli","TorsorDelooping.Delooping.torsorLoopEquivGroup"],"source":"src/TorsorDelooping/Delooping.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.Homotopy.Connected","Cubical.HITs.Truncation.Properties"]}
{"id":"regular-sip-composition","statement":"For regular-torsor right translations, the SIP loop paths satisfy p (g · h) ≡ p g ∙ p h.","local":["TorsorDelooping.SIPCoherence.regularTorsorLoop","TorsorDelooping.SIPCoherence.regularTorsorLoop-comp"],"source":"src/TorsorDelooping/SIPCoherence.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.Foundations.Univalence.uaCompEquiv","Cubical.Foundations.GroupoidLaws"]}
{"id":"lifted-em1-torsor-equivalence","statement":"The universe-lifted library delooping LiftedEM₁ G is equivalent as a type to LeftTorsorModuli ℓ G.","local":["TorsorDelooping.UniverseLiftedComparison.LiftedEM₁","TorsorDelooping.UniverseLiftedComparison.liftedEm1ToTorsorEquiv"],"source":"src/TorsorDelooping/UniverseLiftedComparison.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.HITs.EilenbergMacLane1.rec'","Cubical.Homotopy.EilenbergMacLane.Properties.ΩEM₁Iso","Cubical.Homotopy.WhiteheadsLemma.ΩEquiv→Equiv","Cubical.Foundations.Prelude.Lift"]}
{"id":"lifted-path-torsor-characterization","statement":"Given PointedLoopGroupData G BG pt, Lift (lsuc ℓ) BG is equivalent as a type to LeftTorsorModuli ℓ G.","local":["TorsorDelooping.PathTorsor.PointedLoopGroupData","TorsorDelooping.PathTorsor.pathTorsor","TorsorDelooping.PathTorsor.liftedPathTorsorModuliEquiv"],"source":"src/TorsorDelooping/PathTorsor.agda","kind":"local theorem","upstream":["Cubical.Homotopy.Connected","Cubical.Homotopy.WhiteheadsLemma.ΩEquiv→Equiv","Cubical.Foundations.Univalence"]}
